00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:37,360
for not conducting the activities in the outdoors

726
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:40,120
that we do in a responsible way.

727
00:32:40,120 --> 00:32:42,120
So there's a lot we can do

728
00:32:42,120 --> 00:32:46,280
to make the activities we're doing a little bit safer.

729
00:32:46,280 --> 00:32:49,040
But at the end of the day, there is always gonna be risk

730
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:51,120
and every trip that goes out

731
00:32:51,120 --> 00:32:55,240
should have some level of a risk management plan.

732
00:32:55,240 --> 00:32:58,040
What are the likely hazards

733
00:32:58,040 --> 00:33:01,400
that are gonna be encountered in? really, three areas.

734
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:04,440
One, the particular environment we're in.

735
00:33:04,440 --> 00:33:06,280
is there gonna be a big river crossing

736
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:08,120
we're gonna have to do

737
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:10,120
and potentially could the water be high

738
00:33:10,120 --> 00:33:11,200
on that river crossing?

739
00:33:11,200 --> 00:33:15,520
and then the activity we're doing is,

740
00:33:15,520 --> 00:33:19,640
if it's backpacking, is one of the hazards

741
00:33:19,640 --> 00:33:23,160
maybe lightning up on a peak or a ridge,

742
00:33:23,160 --> 00:33:28,080
or is it swimming in a remote cold pond lake?

743
00:33:28,080 --> 00:33:30,040
and then hazards within the group-

744
00:33:30,040 --> 00:33:32,399
and that's a really important one-

745
00:33:32,399 --> 00:33:35,080
is looking at your who's going

746
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:37,600
and thinking about the physical,

747
00:33:37,600 --> 00:33:42,320
emotional, health needs of the participants in that group

748
00:33:42,320 --> 00:33:45,840
and are there special steps you need to take for those

749
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:48,080
Everything you identify as a risk?

750
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:53,320
there's a little process of kind of figuring out:

751
00:33:53,320 --> 00:33:57,120
can we, is there a way we can reduce the risk?

752
00:33:57,120 --> 00:34:00,160
Can we eliminate it potentially

753
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:02,840
if it's not important to the activity,

754
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:06,040
or can we just say that that's an inherent risk

755
00:34:06,040 --> 00:34:08,440
that we need to accept as part of this.

756
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:09,960
So looking at those things

757
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:12,240
and thinking about how can you modify them

758
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:14,360
without taking all the fun out of it.

759
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:16,440
there's the looking at things in advance

760
00:34:16,440 --> 00:34:17,880
and how are you gonna deal with them,

761
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:22,320
knowing how to respond if something does go wrong.

762
00:34:22,480 --> 00:34:27,480
This just isn't because there is a fear of being sued

763
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:31,440
or some kind of liability problem or something like that.

764
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:35,240
this is for real and this is how you know

765
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:37,480
you can kill people if you don't do this.

766
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:38,320
Is it kind of?

767
00:34:38,320 --> 00:34:40,640
And that's a tricky balancing act.

768
00:34:40,640 --> 00:34:42,520
People often view this safety stuff

769
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:45,920
as being driven by the liability thing,

770
00:34:45,920 --> 00:34:48,920
but I work with some of the best lawyers

771
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:53,520
who specialize, actually, in defending organizations

772
00:34:53,520 --> 00:34:57,400
from lawsuits and they all, front and center, tell you

773
00:34:58,600 --> 00:35:01,880
that don't bother with any of this stuff-

774
00:35:01,880 --> 00:35:04,000
the safety stuff in risk management-

775
00:35:04,000 --> 00:35:06,080
if all you're concerned about is being sued.

776
00:35:06,080 --> 00:35:09,240
you do it because you care about the people

777
00:35:09,240 --> 00:35:11,920
you're taking into the outdoors

778
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:14,600
and that you wanna provide these experiences,

779
00:35:14,600 --> 00:35:17,920
but you also wanna do it in a conscientious manner.

780
00:35:17,920 --> 00:35:20,120
It takes a bit of an ego to be a scout leader

781
00:35:21,480 --> 00:35:24,040
and there's a lot of bravado involved

782
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:25,480
and things like that,

783
00:35:25,480 --> 00:35:26,960
and I think it's particularly valuable

784
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:28,200
having someone like yourself

785
00:35:28,200 --> 00:35:29,920
who has a little perspective on this

786
00:35:29,920 --> 00:35:32,640
and who actually studies these things,

787
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:36,120
to back up the idea that this is really important.

788
00:35:36,120 --> 00:35:37,840
There are some hazards out there.

789
00:35:37,840 --> 00:35:40,120
it's not disproportionate.

790
00:35:40,120 --> 00:35:43,160
I mean, if you look at some statistical information,

791
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:47,840
other activities these teens could be doing

